'''Leila Martins Carvalho''' ({{IPA|pt|ˈlej.lɐ maʁˈtʃ ı˜s kaʁˈva.ʎu}}; born 8 August 1960) is a former [[Balisca|Baliscan]] politician who served as the 40th [[Secretary General of Balisca]], from 4 January 1998 to 4 January 2007. A member of the [[Reformist Bloc (Balisca)|Reformist Bloc]], she became the first Secretary General (of three) to be aligned with the [[W:platformism|platform]] before it's dissolution in 2022.

Carvalho ran in, and ultimately won, the [[1997 Baliscan premiership election|1997 premiership election]], buoyed by her advocacy as a congressional delegate for limited economic opening and gradual integration with the emerging [[W:Liberal international order|liberal international order]]. Her tenure would see Balisca's accession to [[W:Mercosur|Mercosur]] and the [[W:World Trade Organization|World Trade Organization]].

